# Supabase configuration for the browser client.
#
# Only the project URL and the PUBLISHABLE (anon) key belong here. They are safe to
# ship to the browser because Row Level Security (RLS) on every table scopes access
# to the single signed-in owner account (see specs/004-supabase-data-migration/contracts/schema.sql).
#
# NEVER put the Supabase SECRET (service_role) key in this file, in any .env* file,
# or anywhere else that ends up in the browser bundle or the git repo. It is not
# needed by this app at all.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Craft Tutorial Links (spec 008-craft-tutorial-links): the YouTube Data API key is NOT a
# browser env var for the same reason as above — it's a project-level secret with a shared
# quota, not something to ship to every visitor's browser. Instead it's read by the
# `youtube-metadata` Supabase Edge Function (supabase/functions/youtube-metadata/index.ts),
# which the browser calls via supabase.functions.invoke() and never sees the key itself.
#
# Set it on the Supabase project (not here) with:
#   supabase secrets set YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your-key-here
#   supabase functions deploy youtube-metadata
